e position was gone in one move."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "C2 started a long run of White moves on the lower left and bottom edge that each lost around 19 to 22 points. The lead hovered between roughly +19 and +40 for Black across moves 34 to 56, because both sides kept trading the same large swing."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script that ran only parsed returned boards (game-086-inspection.js: groups, liberties, regions, area), counted a fixed coordinate target, replayed the already-played actual moves to check legality and captures (game-086-verification.js), or wrote logs, SGF and notes. Nothing looped over empty points to score candidates or played hypothetical continuations, so no code chose or ranked moves.", "stop": false}}